# Template: capability. An outcome some actor gets; it owns the flows,
# sequences, and single-use rules and triggers that name it.
# Required: ready, kind, id, name, summary, outcome, actors (who gets the outcome).
# Optional: order (position on the product page), dcl {level 1-10, basis}.
# Omit dcl to use the product default; if neither is set, there is none.
# An own basis explains why the level differs; equal levels warn as dcl.same.
ready: 2
kind: capability
id: notes
display_id: CAP-NOTES
name: Notes
summary: A person writes notes, keeps them, and deletes the ones they no longer want.
outcome: A person writes a note and finds it again later.
actors:
  - actor.person
order: 1
dcl:
  level: 4
  basis: >-
    People rely on saved notes between visits, so saving and reopening them
    need core-path reliability and common-failure recovery beyond the pilot default.
